 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Authentication UI
+
+Sign-in supports passkey autofill and explicit passkey authentication. Sign-up
+keeps password account creation and offers passkey registration after sign-in.
+Account settings are available at `/devtools-times/account` and support passkey
+creation, listing, renaming, deletion, and identity verification for sensitive changes.
+
+The authentication backend is external to this repository. See
+[the passkey API contract](docs/passkey-api.md) for required endpoints, session
+behavior, and server verification requirements. Configure `PUBLIC_AUTH_API_URL`
+at build time to use a compatible service; see `.env.example`.
diff --git a/docs/passkey-api.md b/docs/passkey-api.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a185a03
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/passkey-api.md
@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+# Passkey UI integration
+
+The React UI uses the existing authentication service. It does not fabricate accounts,
+credentials, verification results, or sessions in local storage. Set
+`PUBLIC_AUTH_API_URL` to override the existing remote API URL at build time.
+**The backend implementation is outside this repository. The endpoints below must
+be provided by that service before passkey flows can work end to end.**
+
+Every request uses `credentials: include` and `cache: no-store`. The service must
+issue a Secure, HttpOnly session cookie. For cross-origin hosting, configure an
+explicit allowed frontend origin, credentialed CORS (including OPTIONS), and an
+appropriate SameSite cookie policy. Deploy frontend and API on the same site where
+possible because browsers can block third-party cookies. Protect every mutation
+against CSRF with server-side Origin validation (and a CSRF token if required by
+the deployment). Do not accept wildcard CORS origins. Existing password APIs must
+establish this session on login; a JSON token alone is insufficient for this UI.
+
+Responses are JSON. Non-2xx responses use `{ "error": "Safe user-facing message" }`.
+Use 401 for an expired session, 403 for denied or expired reauthentication, and 404
+with `code: "CREDENTIAL_NOT_FOUND"` for a specifically unknown credential on
+authentication verification. Avoid account
+existence disclosures. Do not return 404 for an unimplemented verification route:
+it would incorrectly tell the browser that an existing credential is unknown.
+
+| Method | Path | Request | Successful response |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| POST | `/register` | `{username,password}` | Account created; existing password contract |
+| POST | `/login` | `{username,password}` | Establish session; existing password contract |
+| POST | `/logout` | `{}` | Revoke session |
+| GET | `/account` | — | `{name,displayName,hasPassword}` |
+| PUT | `/account` | `{name,displayName}` | Updated account plus `{rpId,userId}` |
+| GET | `/passkeys` | — | `{rpId,userId,credentials:[...]}` |
+| PUT | `/passkeys/:id` | `{name}` | Renamed record |
+| DELETE | `/passkeys/:id` | `{}` | Successful deletion |
+| POST | `/passkeys/register/options` | `{promotion:boolean}` | WebAuthn creation options JSON |
+| POST | `/passkeys/register/verify` | Native credential `.toJSON()` | Successful verified registration |
+| POST | `/passkeys/authenticate/options` | `{}` | WebAuthn request options JSON |
+| POST | `/passkeys/authenticate/verify` | Native credential `.toJSON()` | Establish session |
+| POST | `/passkeys/reauth/options` | `{}` | Account-constrained WebAuthn request options JSON |
+| POST | `/passkeys/reauth/verify` | Native credential `.toJSON()` | Mark session recently verified |
+| POST | `/reauth/password` | `{password}` | Mark session recently verified |
+
+Credential rows contain `id` (Base64URL), `name` (custom label), `aaguid`,
+`registeredAt` (epoch milliseconds), optional `lastUsedAt` (epoch milliseconds),
+`providerName` and `providerIcon` (PNG data URI). Derive provider hints from a vetted
+AAGUID registry; use “Unknown passkey provider” for zero/unknown AAGUIDs. AAGUID is
+for display only and must never influence authorization. Store public keys,
+transports, signature counters, device type and backup state server-side as well.
+Never expose public-key internals through the list endpoint. `userId` is the opaque
+WebAuthn user handle, not the account's username. All signal IDs must be unpadded
+Base64URL, never display names or human-readable database placeholders.
+
+## Required server guarantees
+
+Use a vetted WebAuthn library (e.g. SimpleWebAuthn server), durable credential storage,
+and a configured RP ID and allowed origin list. Generate high-entropy, expiring,
+one-use challenges tied to the requesting session and ceremony type. Persist the
+user verification policy alongside each challenge; enforce that policy during
+verification along with challenge, signature, origin, RP ID and presence checks.
+Consume challenges atomically and update signature counters safely.
+
+Registration requires an authenticated session with recent verification. Generate
+`excludeCredentials` from existing account credentials and require discoverable
+credentials (`residentKey: required`, `requireResidentKey: true`). Promotions use
+`authenticatorAttachment: platform`; settings registration omits attachment to allow
+security keys. Match `requireUserVerification` to the stored policy (false for
+preferred, true for required). Do not commit credentials until verified.
+
+Primary authentication uses `allowCredentials: []`. Resolve the returned credential
+to its account only after verification and rotate the authenticated session.
+Reauthentication must use a **nonempty** allow-list containing only the active
+account's registered credentials, enforce ownership during verification, and must
+never switch accounts. Require user verification for sensitive changes.
+
+Require a short-lived recent-verification session grant for registration, profile
+changes and deletion. The UI always requests fresh verification before these
+operations; server checks remain authoritative. Bind the grant to the active session,
+expire it, and reject stale grants. Enforce ownership for all credential operations
+and prevent deletion of the final sign-in method (including concurrent deletions).
+A newly established password session may permit the post-signup promotion.
+
+The UI aborts autofill before explicit actions and on unmount, handles user
+cancellation without changing account state, and feature-detects capabilities.
+`webauthn-polyfills` supplies native JSON helpers and capability checks on older
+browsers. Password manager signals are optional, nonfatal enhancements; accepted
+credential lists sync on settings load and deletion, and user detail updates sync
+after profile changes. Passkey nickname changes do not signal user detail updates.
